description:
container/container.go ends with a doc comment for a Close method that has no body:

  // Close stops background goroutines owned by services in the container
  // (e.g. peer cleanup, contract cache TTL cleaner). Safe to call multiple times.

There is no such method, and nothing calls it. Verified: grep for 'func (c *Container)' finds only SetSmartContractHandler, and the build succeeds with no caller.

So the goroutines the comment claims are stopped are not stopped. ContractCache does have a Stop() with a done channel (storage/smart_contract/contract_cache.go), and PeerService starts a cleanup goroutine, but nothing invokes either on shutdown. This is the same class as stargate-gkh, which fixed BlockMonitor and Orchestrator lifecycles, and was missed because the comment reads as though the work were already done.

Fix: implement Close() to stop the cache cleaner and peer cleanup, and defer it in runHTTPServer alongside agentOrch.Stop() and blockMonitor.Stop(). Found while writing container DI tests for stargate-a49.
